   "total_units 36 is the printed 'Total Units' in the Unit Requirements table: Prerequisite Award 18 (Building Construction Certificate of Achievement) plus Required Courses 18. The second award's own course requirement is 18 units; reviewer should confirm whether 36 or 18 is the intended award total.",
   "The prerequisite certificate's requirements (required CNST A165, CNST A195 or CNST A194, and 12 units of restricted electives) are recorded as blocks because the page prints them under 'Required Prerequisites' and counts them in the 36-unit total.",
   "Course units are printed only for CNST A165 (3) and CNST A195 (3); elective lists print no units, so units are null. The trailing '1' after 'Construction Safety/CAL OSHA' is a footnote marker ('Required for First Certificate'), not units.",
   "No course may be applied to more than one certificate, so courses used for the first award cannot count toward the 18 units of the second award.",
   "ARCH/CNST A196 and ARCH/CNST A197 are cross-listed codes matched to closed-list CNST A196 and CNST A197.",
   "Catalog CNST A211 (Decorative Concrete) matched to closed-list entry 'CNSTA211 Decorative Concret'.",
